{
  "analysis": "The build failed because my_stdlib.h includes `<stdint.h>` but we're using `-nostdinc` so only our compat directory is available. I need to either include the GCC freestanding headers or create a compat `stdint.h` that provides the standard integer types. The GCC cross-compiler has freestanding headers at its include path.",
  "plan": "Add the GCC freestanding include directory to the include path, or create a compat stdint.h/stddef.h/stdarg.h/stdbool.h. The simplest approach is to add `-isystem $(mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -print-file-name=include)` to CFLAGS, which provides stdint.h, stddef.h, stdarg.h, and stdbool.h without pulling in system libc headers.",
  "str": "Update build.sh to add the GCC freestanding include directory, then rerun the build.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's|-Icompat -Icompat/sys -I.|-Icompat -Icompat/sys -I. -isystem $(mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -print-file-name=include)|' build.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "./build.sh\n",
      "duration": 10.0
    }
  ]
}
